From 150367aeb01cc567d909ca4d904eff97f6cc3cb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:40:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [clangd] Memoize module file validation across requests

Validating a built module file re-hashes all of its input files for
every request that reuses the same prerequisite modules, so completion
on a file importing many modules re-validates the whole set on every
keystroke even when nothing changed.

Validation now goes through a bounded memo keyed by the published BMI,
the dependency chain, and the (size, mtime) identity of every input the
validation read. A later request re-stats those files and reuses the
verdict when none of them moved; any drift falls back to a full
validation. Validations whose inputs were read through an overlay
buffer are not memoized.

To keep the memo key stable across requests, validation reads the
published BMIs rather than the per-request copy-on-read views, and a
copy may be validated through its published source while that source is
unchanged.
---
