+# The validation cache reuses the up-to-date verdict of a published BMI
+# across requests instead of re-validating it on every preamble-compatibility
+# check. The driver builds a module project and requests three completions on
+# the same file, each after a body-only edit that keeps the preamble valid:
+# round 1 builds and validates cold; round 2 re-validates cold (the
+# dependency chain now contains the module itself); round 3 must hit the
+# validation cache. The driver asserts both transitions in clangd's log.
+#
+# UNSUPPORTED: system-windows
+#
+# RUN: rm -fr %t
+# RUN: mkdir -p %t
+# RUN: %python %p/Inputs/modules-cache-driver.py clangd %t %clang
